{
  "mn64:0.1": "Middle Discourses 64 ",
  "mn64:0.2": "The Longer Discourse With Māluṅkya ",
  "mn64:1.1": "So I have heard. ",
  "mn64:1.2": "At one time the Buddha was staying near Sāvatthī in Jeta’s Grove, Anāthapiṇḍika’s monastery. ",
  "mn64:1.3": "There the Buddha addressed the mendicants, ",
  "mn64:1.4": "“Mendicants!” ",
  "mn64:1.5": "“Venerable sir,” they replied. ",
  "mn64:1.6": "The Buddha said this: ",
  "mn64:2.1": "“Mendicants, do you remember the five lower fetters taught by me?” ",
  "mn64:2.2": "When he said this, Venerable Māluṅkyaputta said to him, ",
  "mn64:2.3": "“Sir, I remember them.” ",
  "mn64:2.4": "“But how do you remember them?” ",
  "mn64:2.5": "“I remember the lower fetters taught by the Buddha as follows: substantialist view, ",
  "mn64:2.6": "doubt, ",
  "mn64:2.7": "misapprehension of precepts and observances, ",
  "mn64:2.8": "sensual desire, ",
  "mn64:2.9": "and ill will. ",
  "mn64:2.10": "That’s how I remember the five lower fetters taught by the Buddha.” ",
  "mn64:3.1": "“Who on earth do you remember being taught the five lower fetters in that way? ",
  "mn64:3.2": "Wouldn’t the wanderers of other religions fault you using the simile of the infant? ",
  "mn64:3.3": "For a little baby doesn’t even have a concept of ‘substantial reality’, so how could substantialist view possibly arise in them? ",
  "mn64:3.4": "Yet the underlying tendency to substantialist view still lies within them. ",
  "mn64:3.5": "A little baby